Visual Studio 2026 with no Visual Studio 2022 installed: build the vc17 presets
with the VS 2026 generator and VS 2022's v143 toolset (VS 2026's "MSVC v143"
component), so the SDK is the same as from VS 2022 -- vc143 libraries, and CUDA
12.x still works (VS 2026's own v145 needs CUDA 13.2+, which needs R580+
drivers). Machines with VS 2022 (full or Build Tools) generate exactly as before.

Flow: its vs2022 projects ask for v143, but build.bat points premake at the
newest Visual Studio's default toolset; on VS 2026 that's v145, whose headers
v143 can't compile with. Use the v143 component's toolset folder there.

diff --git a/flow/build.bat b/flow/build.bat
index 4154e31..09a2ac7 100644
--- a/flow/build.bat
+++ b/flow/build.bat
@@ -46,6 +46,12 @@ if exist "%InstallDir%\VC\Auxiliary\Build\Microsoft.VCToolsVersion.default.txt"
 )
 endlocal & set "MSVS_TOOLSET=%MSVS_TOOLSET%"
 
+:: godot_physx: the vs2022 projects ask for the v143 toolset, which Visual Studio 2026 (18) has as its "MSVC v143"
+:: component; use that toolset's headers and libraries too, not VS 2026's v145 default, which v143 can't compile with.
+if "%MAJOR_VERSION%" GEQ "18" (
+    for /d %%d in ("%InstallDir%\VC\Tools\MSVC\14.3*" "%InstallDir%\VC\Tools\MSVC\14.4*") do set "MSVS_TOOLSET=%%~d"
+)
+
 if not exist "%MSVS_TOOLSET%" (
     echo MSVC toolset not found, check Visual Studio installation
     goto Error
